{
  "esm": "2.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "mom6_sadourny_pvf",
    "description": "The SADOURNY75_ENERGY potential-vorticity flux at one C-grid velocity face (MOM_CoriolisAdv.F90 CorAdCalc :724-726 for CAu, :951-953 for CAv): pvf = 0.25*(((q_a*(f_a1 + f_a2)) + (q_b*(f_b1 + f_b2)))*I_d), the two q-points a/b at the ends of the face, each times the sum of the two transverse layer volume fluxes adjacent to it, scaled by the face's 1/length I_d. ONE law for both faces: mom6_cgrid_pvf_u binds q_a = q(I,J), f_a = vh(i+1,J), vh(i,J), q_b = q(I,J-1), f_b = vh(i,J-1), vh(i+1,J-1), I_d = IdxCu(I,j); mom6_cgrid_pvf_v binds q_a = q(I-1,J), f_a = uh(I-1,j), uh(I-1,j+1), q_b = q(I,J), f_b = uh(I,j), uh(I,j+1), I_d = IdyCv(i,J) and negates the result. At a solid wall the rules bind the fluxes through the closed wall faces (and through land faces beyond the domain) to 0, so a q-point term whose two fluxes are wall fluxes vanishes, as MOM6's zero wall fluxes make it. Pure scalar algebra, [L T-2].",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["esd:stencil", "family:mom6_cgrid", "grid:mom6_cgrid", "op:pvf"],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Sadourny, R. (1975). The dynamics of finite-difference models of the shallow-water equations. Journal of the Atmospheric Sciences, 32(4), 680-689.",
        "doi": "10.1175/1520-0469(1975)032<0680:TDOFDM>2.0.CO;2"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Adcroft, A., et al. (2019). The GFDL global ocean and sea ice model OM4.0. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 11(10), 3167-3211.",
        "doi": "10.1029/2019MS001726"
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "mom6_sadourny_pvf": {
      "params": ["q_a", "f_a1", "f_a2", "q_b", "f_b1", "f_b2", "I_d"],
      "description": "The SADOURNY75_ENERGY PV flux at one velocity face (MOM_CoriolisAdv.F90:724-726, :951-953)",
      "body": {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
          { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": 0.25, "units": "1" },
          {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  { "op": "*", "args": ["q_a", { "op": "+", "args": ["f_a1", "f_a2"] }] },
                  { "op": "*", "args": ["q_b", { "op": "+", "args": ["f_b1", "f_b2"] }] }
                ]
              },
              "I_d"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
